netdomain membership: discovery opens TCP to :1400 and UDP SSDP; Android requires every socket-creating domain to reach netd fwmarkd (on-device 2026-11-25: denied { write } name="fwmarkd" scontext=hal_audio_sonos (the retired daemon; the module in hal_audio_default needs the same)). netdomain is the standard attribute that grants it, as used by the wifi/rild HALs in this same policy.
append/etc/selinux/vendor_service_contexts: IModule/sonos fell back to default_android_service, which audioserver may not find (avc find, build 20261126T003439Z). Label it hal_audio_service like every other IModule.
property set rules + files/etc/init/audio-sonos.rc: audioserver reads module ports once at boot, before the network is up (build 20261126T005544Z served 0 rooms while discovery later found 11). The HAL sets vendor.sonos.rooms_gen when the background search finds a player it has not listed (5 s settle); the rc restarts the HAL, whose start-up search lists it. No amp list is stored.
vendor_property_contexts persist.vendor.sonos.amp.: builds up to v1.7 saved the amp list there; the module blanks any such entries at start, which needs the label. Nothing is written there otherwise.
vendor_property_contexts vendor.sonos.name. + vendor_public_default_prop set: the HAL publishes each player's room name by IP; system_server (which may read vendor_public_default_prop) names each output route from it, since audio policy drops device port names.
Sonos rooms are a module in the reference audio service (hal_audio_default): it gets the network (SSDP discovery, UPnP control, HTTP stream) and property-set rights the standalone daemon had; the daemon and its rc are removed.
remove etc/selinux/precompiled_sepolicy*: the base (v1.2) ships a precompiled policy, which init loads instead of compiling vendor_sepolicy.cil when its hashes match; removing it makes init compile the policy, so the rules above take effect.
dontaudit hal_camera_default/hal_graphics_composer_default search on system_data_file: NXP's Vivante GPU driver (libGAL.so) builds /data/data/<process name> from /proc/self/cmdline at start-up to look for a per-app cache; a HAL has no such directory and /data/data is labelled per-user (s0:c512,c768). The lookup is refused and the driver carries on. Silenced, nothing granted.
dontaudit init-insmod-sh module_load on system_lib_file and ioctl on its own exec: NXP's module script also tries modules under /system/lib/modules (rfkill, 9pnet, 8021q, 6lowpan, pps_core) that this panel does not use, and runs ls on early.init.cfg. Refused, harmless. Silenced, nothing granted.
dontaudit hal_sensors_default binder call to system_server: a sensor HAL callback the platform does not allow; sensors keep working (ttsensor reads the steam room sensor). Silenced, nothing granted.
dontaudit vendor_init property set on build_prop/default_prop/future_pm_prop: /vendor/build.prop sets ro.adb.secure, persist.adb.tcp.port and pm.dexopt.boot, which Android 15 reserves to the system. The first two already hold the intended values from the system side (adb works on 5555); pm.dexopt.boot keeps its default. Silenced; granting vendor_init these would weaken a deliberate protection.
plat-sepolicy.cil.add (appended to the system image's plat_sepolicy.cil; plat_sepolicy_and_mapping.sha256 is recomputed to match). dontaudit only, nothing granted:
  bootanim search system_data_file: the same Vivante GPU driver /data/data/<process> lookup, from the boot animation.
  init write debugfs_wifi_tracing/debugfs_bootreceiver_tracing: the vendor init script switching on kernel trace events init may not write.
  gmscore_app read adbd_prop/system_adbd_prop: Google Play services checking whether adb is enabled.
  system_app write apk_data_file, search privapp_data_file: the settings app and Google services touching app data directories.
  system_suspend read sysfs: wakeup statistics under /sys/devices/.../wakeup0.
  toolbox ioctl ram_device: mkswap probing the zram block device.
